ia, Vila do Conde, Póvoa de Varzim and Espinho. The city is built at the high ground overlooking the Douro River estuary's northern side, and its historical centre was declared a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1996. It has been continuously inhabited since at least the 4th century BC.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Porto","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Porto","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Porto is the second city of Portugal, stacked above the Douro estuary and known for its wine. The Dom Luis I Bridge, Porto Cathedral and the Palacio da Bolsa lead the sights, and ten hours covers them. June to August is the warm season.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":252687,"visit_h":7.2}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-casa-da-musica","name":"Casa da Música","kind":"Theatre","lat":41.15889,"lon":-8.63071,"dist_km":2.0,"rank_score":10.9,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-estadio-do-dragao","name":"Estádio do Dragão","kind":"Landmark","lat":41.16176,"lon":-8.58393,"dist_km":2.7,"rank_score":10.25,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Est%C3%A1dio_do_Drag%C3%A3o_%288468978586%29.jpg/960px-Est%C3%A1dio_do_Drag%C3%A3o_%288468978586%29.jpg","author":"Edgar Jiménez from Porto, Portugal","licence":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Est%C3%A1dio_do_Drag%C3%A3o_(8468978586).jpg","w":2560,"h":1920,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-luiz-i-bridge","name":"Luiz I Bridge","kind":"Bridge","lat":41.13972,"lon":-8.60944,"dist_km":1.0,"rank_score":9.58,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Puente_Don_Luis_I%2C_Oporto%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_13.JPG/960px-Puente_Don_Luis_I%2C_Oporto%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_13.JPG","author":"Diego Delso","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://common